<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<assembly xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v1" manifestVersion="1.0">
  <!--
    SYSTEM DPI awareness, deliberately not PerMonitorV2.

    Per-monitor awareness makes Windows send WM_DPICHANGED as the window crosses to a screen with
    different scaling, and Slint mishandles the rescale: the window jumps size and the content is
    drawn at the wrong scale inside it. That is slint-ui/slint#11073 (open, marked upstream) and
    rust-windowing/winit#3040 - not something this app can fix.

    With system awareness the window is never asked to rescale. It keeps one size and Windows
    composites it for the other screen, so dragging between monitors is stable. The cost is that
    it can look slightly soft on a monitor whose scaling differs from the system setting, which is
    a far better trade than the window resizing and rendering incorrectly.
  -->
  <application xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v3">
    <windowsSettings>
      <dpiAware xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/SMI/2005/WindowsSettings">true</dpiAware>
    </windowsSettings>
  </application>
  <compatibility xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:compatibility.v1">
    <application>
      <!-- Windows 10 and 11 -->
      <supportedOS Id="{8e0f7a12-bfb3-4fe8-b9a5-48fd50a15a9a}" />
    </application>
  </compatibility>
</assembly>
